.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_EXECUTE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_execute ,
.Nm dtfl_execute_directly ,
.Nm dtfl_guards_join
.Nd run a timely dataflow computation
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_execute "const dtfl_config *cfg" "dtfl_worker_fn fn" "void *ctx" "dtfl_guards **guards"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_execute_directly "dtfl_worker_fn fn" "void *ctx"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_guards_join "dtfl_guards *guards"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_execute
starts the workers described by
.Fa cfg
and runs
.Fa fn
on each, passing it the worker handle and
.Fa ctx .
Each worker builds its dataflows in
.Fa fn ,
then steps until no dataflows remain.
The same
.Fa fn
runs on every worker, so it must build the same dataflows in the same
order on each.
.Pp
When
.Fa guards
is
.Dv NULL ,
.Fn dtfl_execute
waits for every worker to finish before returning.
When it is not
.Dv NULL ,
the call returns once the workers have started and stores a
.Vt dtfl_guards
handle through
.Fa guards ;
the caller must then call
.Fn dtfl_guards_join
to wait for completion and release the handle.
Until it returns, the running workers and network threads still use
.Fa cfg ,
.Fa ctx
and every log subscriber's context, so the caller must keep them valid
until then.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_execute_directly
runs
.Fa fn
on a single worker on the calling thread, the equivalent of
.Fn dtfl_execute
with a default
.Vt dtfl_config .
.Pp
The communication mode in
.Fa cfg
selects the runtime: a single thread, several threads in one process,
or the seeded simulator.
See
.Xr dtfl_config 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return 0 on success, or one of the errors below.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void worker(dtfl_worker *w, void *ctx) {
	dtfl_worker_dataflow(w, "example", ctx, build, NULL);
}

dtfl_config *cfg = dtfl_config_new();
dtfl_config_set_threads(cfg, 4);
dtfl_config_set_mode(cfg, DTFL_COMM_PROCESS);
if (dtfl_execute(cfg, worker, tc, NULL) != 0)
	errx(1, "%s", dtfl_last_error_detail());
dtfl_config_free(cfg);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_ENOTSUP
.It Bq Er DTFL_EINVAL
.Fa cfg
or
.Fa fn
is
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er DTFL_ENOTSUP
The configured communication mode is not available in this build.
.It Bq Er DTFL_EIO
A worker or network thread could not be started.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_config 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute_worker 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn execute ,
.Fn execute_directly
and the
.Vt WorkerGuards
returned by
.Fn execute .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
.Fn dtfl_execute
and
.Fn dtfl_execute_directly
are called once from a controlling thread.
The worker handle each passes to
.Fa fn
belongs to that worker's thread and must not be shared.
.Fn dtfl_guards_join
is called from the thread that received the handle.
